    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on **Corbin Carroll** (83.27) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.74), who represent our highest-upside plays tonight. **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime spot against McGreevy, benefiting from a massive boost due to his top-tier order placement and an favorable platoon split. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** is positioned to exploit a generous park factor and a favorable matchup against Singer; his 14% boost from dynamic platoon indicators makes him a core component of today\u2019s production floor. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (75.01) also anchors the lineup, as the combination of his power profile and a double-digit boost from his platoon advantage against King ensures he remains an essential start.\n\nWhile our starting lineup is robust, **Josh Naylor** (58.63) was the toughest exclusion. Despite his strong base projection, he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to **Kyle Karros** (60.20), whose massive 14% park boost gave him the edge in a day where marginal gains in environment dictate the final roster construction. We remain cautious regarding **James Wood** (66.63); although his xwOBA remains elite and his park factor is stellar, he faces a high-risk scenario against a pitcher with an elite catcher pop time and a strong hold capability that could suppress his SB floor. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing** and **Edwin Arroyo** closely, as their sub-50 scores combined with their lower batting order spots make them candidates to be swapped if official lineups shift, though we are currently comfortable letting them ride.",
